s"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Falling Intonation</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you ask a question with <span class=\"strong\">where, when, what, which, why, what </span> or <span class=\"strong\">how, </span> your voice falls at the end."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Rising Intonation</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If the question is a yes/no question, the voice rises at the end."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:  What about you?<br /><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  I like tennis. It's my favorite sport."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Does your family like sports?<br /> <span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  Yes, my father really likes sports."}, {"type": "text", "content": "</br>The stress is usually placed on the last word in questions.</br> </br>Examples:</br> Are you going to the <span class = \"strong\">game</span>?</br> When does it <span class = \"strong\">start</span>?"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cup "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a container to hold liquid "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Do you like your cappuccino in a cup or a mug?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le03ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear in a coffee shop."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mug "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large cup"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: I use a mug for my coffee in the morning."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le03ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lineup "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "people waiting in a line to be served "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There is a long lineup. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le03ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hungry "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "feeling the need to eat "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm not hungry."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le03ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dad  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "father "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My dad really likes sports."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le03ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mom "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "mother"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My mom doesn't like it when my dad watches football on TV."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le03ob04aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sports "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an organized game "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Does your family like sports? "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le03ob04aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "favorite "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the most liked  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's my favorite sport."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le03ob04aud08"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn2le03ob04re1img01.png"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, say these short <span class=\"italic\">a</span>, short <span class=\"italic\">i</span> and short 